course: dictionary
lesson: 3379
title: Exile: far from home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exile means being forced to live away from your own country, often as a punishment or to stay safe. «In the Ramayana Rama goes into exile (sent away to live far from home) to keep his father's word.» The words in brackets give you the meaning, so you can check it in the sentence.
explain: Exile can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, exile is the state of living away, and an exile is a person who does. As a verb, to exile someone means to send them away and not let them return. Look at how the word is used: «Orlyk's constitution written in exile» shows the state, not a person.
explain: Look for the phrases around the word: «in exile», «go into exile», «government in exile» and «self-imposed exile». Self-imposed means the person chose it for themselves. The clues around the word tell you whether someone was sent away or decided to leave.
fact: Exile means being forced to live away from your own country, often as a punishment or for safety.
fact: An exile is a person who lives in exile.
fact: To exile someone means to send them away from their country and not let them return.
fact: In the Bible, the Exile is the time when many people of Judah were taken away to Babylon.
fact: Phrases to know: «in exile», «go into exile», «government in exile», «self-imposed exile».
exercise: «In the Ramayana Rama goes into exile.» What does exile mean here? | Coming back home after a war | Building a castle on a hill | *Being sent away to live far from home | Going on a long holiday abroad
exercise: Which word names a person who lives in exile? | A hetman | A psalm | An anthem | *An exile
exercise: «The king decided to exile the prince.» What does exile mean here? | *To send someone away from their country and not let them return | To write a letter to a friend | To sing a song about home | To go on holiday
test: «Orlyk's constitution written in exile» is about a leader's writing. What does in exile mean? | Written in a song for dancing | *Written while living away from their own country | Written in a castle on a hill | Written in a school classroom
test: Which phrase means someone chose to stay away from home by themselves? | government in exile | go into exile | the Exile | *self-imposed exile
exam: What does «exiled» mean in «He was exiled for life»? | Sent a letter home to his family | Given a medal for his bravery | Taken to school every day | *Sent away from his country and not allowed back
